# How a leaf makes sugar
subtitle: "A leaf uses sunlight to build sugar from water and carbon dioxide, so a tree is made mostly of air and water."
tags: ["photosynthesis","plants","biology","chlorophyll","carbon dioxide"]
teaches: ["concepts/photosynthesis"]
thumb: "band \"Trees are made of air\" stamp \"REALLY?\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Charon | a warm, clear teacher, quietly enjoying the idea"}

## How a leaf makes sugar
setting:
    ground: sky/soil/82
    props:
      - {icon: sun, place: top left, size: 70}
      - {icon: seedling, place: along bottom, repeat: 3, size: 40}

    polygon leaf #4f7a3a points [[270,400],[272,414],[278,428],[288,442],[301,455],[318,467],[337,478],[360,487],[385,495],[412,502],[440,506],[470,509],[500,510],[530,509],[560,506],[588,502],[615,495],[640,487],[663,478],[682,467],[699,455],[712,442],[722,428],[728,414],[730,400],[728,386],[722,372],[712,358],[699,345],[682,333],[663,322],[640,313],[615,305],[588,298],[560,294],[530,291],[500,290],[470,291],[440,294],[412,298],[385,305],[360,313],[337,322],[318,333],[301,345],[288,358],[278,372],[272,386]] style.fill #9cc58a style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.35 hidden true
    path rib #4f7a3a points [[270,400],[730,400]] hidden true
    path stem #4f7a3a points [[730,400],[790,320],[810,250]] hidden true
    arrow light #c79a1a from.x 230 from.y 590 to.x 380 to.y 470 hidden true
    text l_light "light" #c79a1a x 160 y 610 hidden true
    arrow water #2f6b8f from.x 810 from.y 250 to.x 700 to.y 385 hidden true
    text l_water "water" #2f6b8f x 880 y 280 hidden true
    arrow co2 #3d3833 from.x 120 from.y 360 to.x 260 to.y 390 hidden true
    text l_co2 "CO₂" #3d3833 x 110 y 320 hidden true
    arrow sugar #b5482e from.x 500 from.y 380 to.x 500 to.y 275 hidden true
    text l_sugar "sugar" #b5482e x 500 y 245 hidden true
    arrow o2 #2f6b8f from.x 640 from.y 460 to.x 760 to.y 560 hidden true
    text l_o2 "O₂" #2f6b8f x 790 y 580 hidden true

How does a plant make its food out of thin air? Look closely at one leaf.
    draw leaf rib stem

Sunlight falls on it. That is the energy for everything that follows.
    draw light l_light

Water comes up through the stem, all the way from the roots.
    draw water l_water

And carbon dioxide drifts in from the air, through tiny pores.
    draw co2 l_co2

Inside, green chlorophyll catches the light and uses its energy to split the water.
    text l_chl "chlorophyll" #4f7a3a x 500 y 430 font_size 22

The hydrogen from the water is joined to the carbon dioxide, and builds sugar, the plant's food.
    draw sugar l_sugar

The oxygen left over from the water goes out into the air, for us to breathe.
    draw o2 l_o2

So a tree's wood is built mostly from air and water, hardly at all from the soil.
    text l_end "wood is mostly air" #3d3833 x 230 y 200

    quiz "A seed of a few grams grows into a tree of many tonnes. Where does most of that mass come from?"
        right: From the air: the carbon in the wood came in as carbon dioxide. Sunlight brings the energy, not the mass.
        * The soil
        + The air, as carbon dioxide
        * The sunlight

A forest is air and water, made solid by sunlight.
    highlight leaf
---
